### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- version: 1.0.2
- > **Published as `imap-smtp-mail` on ClawHub.** The credentials file remains `~/.openclaw/credentials/imap-smtp-email.env` for backward compatibility.
- Create `~/.openclaw/credentials/imap-smtp-email.env` with:
- This skill loads `~/.openclaw/credentials/imap-smtp-email.env` at runtime with `dotenv`. The credential file path can be overridden with the `EMAIL_ENV_FILE` environment variable. The IMAP/SMTP variables do not need to be exported globally in the OpenClaw service environment.
+ version: 1.0.3
+ > **Published as `imap-smtp-mail` on ClawHub.**
+ Create `~/.openclaw/credentials/imap-smtp-mail.env` with:
+ This skill loads `~/.openclaw/credentials/imap-smtp-mail.env` at runtime with `dotenv`. The credential file path can be overridden with the `EMAIL_ENV_FILE` environment variable. The IMAP/SMTP variables do not need to be exported globally in the OpenClaw service environment.

### credentials/imap-smtp-email.example.env  [code]
- # IMAP
- IMAP_HOST=imap.example.com
- IMAP_PORT=993
- IMAP_USER=you@example.com
- IMAP_PASS=change_me
- IMAP_TLS=true
- IMAP_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=true
- IMAP_MAILBOX=INBOX
- IMAP_SAVE_SENT=true
- # IMAP_SENT_MAILBOX=Sent
- # SMTP
- SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
- SMTP_PORT=587
- SMTP_SECURE=false
- SMTP_USER=you@example.com
- SMTP_PASS=change_me
- SMTP_FROM=you@example.com
- SMTP_FROM_NAME=Your Name
- SMTP_REPLY_TO=you@example.com
- SMTP_CLIENT_NAME=example.com
- SMTP_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=true
- # File access controls
- ALLOWED_READ_DIRS=~/.openclaw/workspace,~/.openclaw/workspace/exports,~/.openclaw/workspace/out,~/.openclaw/workspace/tmp
- ALLOWED_WRITE_DIRS=~/.openclaw/workspace/exports,~/.openclaw/workspace/tmp

